1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,769
An investigation rarely suffers from a lack of information.

2
00:00:05,769 --> 00:00:11,075
The real challenge is finding the connections hidden inside it.

3
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:16,331
Meet Veil.

4
00:00:16,331 --> 00:00:24,391
It transforms fragmented investigation records into a structured, connected intelligence network.

5
00:00:24,391 --> 00:00:33,780
This is Operation Trinetra, a synthetic investigation case, moving from documents, to entities, to relationships.

6
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:44,241
Across supported source formats, Veil extracts people, phone numbers, accounts, vehicles and locations.

7
00:00:44,241 --> 00:00:52,304
It preserves the records behind those connections, and brings them into an investigation graph.

8
00:00:52,304 --> 00:00:56,887
Possible identity matches remain open to human review.

9
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:03,322
But visualizing a network isn't enough.

10
00:01:03,322 --> 00:01:12,582
Veil computes paths and surfaces review leads, helping investigators see connections that could be difficult to notice manually.

11
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:21,971
Here, Rahul Sharma connects to Vikram Singh through phones, an intermediary, and bank accounts.

12
00:01:21,971 --> 00:01:25,579
Six hops, spanning multiple source records.

13
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,468
The lead brings communication changes and connected transfers into one reviewable explanation.

14
00:01:35,468 --> 00:01:39,183
A connection to examine, not a conclusion about guilt.

15
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:43,587
And every insight remains explainable.

16
00:01:43,587 --> 00:01:52,279
Instead of presenting a black box conclusion, Veil traces the relationship back to the underlying evidence.

17
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:59,515
Here is the transaction source, its exact row and timestamp, and the original excerpt.

18
00:01:59,515 --> 00:02:03,984
The verification status stays visible alongside the record.

19
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:11,581
The system doesn't decide guilt, and it doesn't replace the investigator.

20
00:02:11,581 --> 00:02:16,579
Identity proposals can be inspected, confirmed, or reversed.

21
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:24,179
Here, the investigator requests more evidence, with a reason preserved in the audit trail.

22
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:36,172
What previously required investigators to manually cross reference records can now become a connected, evidence backed view of an investigation.

23
00:02:36,172 --> 00:02:37,877
A smaller search space.

24
00:02:37,877 --> 00:02:39,137
Meaningful leads.

25
00:02:39,137 --> 00:02:41,286
Human judgment at the center.

26
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:43,502
Veil.

27
00:02:43,502 --> 00:02:48,825
From fragmented evidence to explainable intelligence.